  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Application Scope**\n\nI\'m focusing on defining the scope of this multi-screen application. The navigation spec and design system are guiding me as I determine the initial structure. I am starting by looking at the Organism Encyclopedia and Admin Content Management modules. These will be crucial for the application.\n\n\n**Visualizing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI component visualization, guided by the design system\'s elements. I\'m focusing on color palettes, typography choices, and layout constraints. Specifically, I need to account for the desktop sidebar (280px), the main content area, and the rounded shapes (16px for cards, 8px for inputs). I\'m planning to use a state-based navigation system to manage the application\'s routing. Lucide icons are installed, so a custom navigation state might be safe, instead of installing `react-router`.\n\n\n**Mapping Application Screens**\n\nI\'ve mapped out the main screens: Encyclopedia (with sidebar and 3D viewer), Visualization (full-screen 3D), and Admin (content management). I\'m solidifying the data model, including organism properties. I\'m planning to use placeholders for now, maybe use `image-generation` later to add scientific images.\n\n\n**Implementing Initial Setup**\n\nI\'m now implementing the initial setup, starting with updating `index.css` to import fonts and define the color palette as CSS variables within a Tailwind `@theme` block. I\'ll then create the `src/types.ts` data models, `src/data.ts` mock data, and the necessary UI components within `src/components/...`. Finally, I\'ll structure screens in `src/screens/...` and update `App.tsx` for navigation.\n\n\n**Defining Color Palette**\n\nI have finalized the color palette and defined all key colors as CSS variables, along with font definitions and radius values. I am focusing on making the primary, secondary, and background colors. I\'ve also incorporated the variables into the base layer for application-wide use.\n\n\n**Analyzing Layout & Components**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the attached images to precisely replicate the intended layout and components. I see a consistent structure: a prominent logo, top navigation (Gallery, Library, Notebooks, Settings, Profile), a left sidebar (CELL TYPES, ORGANELLES), and the main content area with a 3D render. The right sidebar focuses on details, notes, and characteristics. This is the new base I will build from.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 68
      nanos: 713111928
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
