  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully built the multi-screen Academic Microbiology Portal, emphasizing a clean, immersive layout with the precise scientific aesthetic described in the design system.\n\n- **Visual Identity & Theme**: Configured the color palette with deep greens (`#012d1d`), mint frosts, and high-contrast charcoal elements. I applied the academic typographic pairings (`Source Serif 4`, `Inter`, `JetBrains Mono`) for a professional look.\n- **Encyclopedia Screen (Gallery)**: Implemented the main viewing layout featuring a sticky taxonomy sidebar and dynamic data presentation. For general cells (like the Animal Cell and Bacillus anthracis), it renders a focused 3D viewport with detailed organism stats. For the Fungi kingdom, it renders an alternate bento-grid layout to display the different types of macroscopic and microscopic fungi.\n- **Visualization Screen (Library)**: Created a dedicated immersive view for interacting with the 3D cell renders, featuring a dark canvas, overlaid toolbars (wireframe, solid, X-ray controls), and ambient lighting.\n- **Admin Management Screen**: Added a clean, table-based content management interface allowing instructors to view, add, or edit organism profiles and manage their publication status.\n- **Assets**: Successfully generated and integrated high-quality 3D renders and macro photography placeholders for the cells and fungi respectively to provide immediate context for the application."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
